A||||4||fotofrank||Alternator replacement?||||9||
Z||000000||fotofrank||07-09-2000||02:53 PM||||Ok, guys, how does the alternator come out of<BR>an '84 SE? I got the bolts out and disconnected everything on the alternator but cannot get it out of the car. The Haynes book says to remove it from ther bottom but no dice. What do I remove to get it out? <P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1.html||||reg||9
Z||000001||ROB MAC||07-09-2000||05:24 PM||||Remove neg. battery cable. Remove the connections at alternator. Remove top and bottom pivot bolt. Rest alt. on engine and remove two bolts and alt. mounting frame. Undo one end of dogbone ,loosen other end and pull it up.<BR>Alternator should pull out but you will have to turn it till you find the easiest way out.<BR>Take it slow and you won't skin your knuckles. After the first time, you should be able to do it in 15-20 min.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fotofrank||07-11-2000||09:39 PM||||ROB MAC, thanks a lot. i got the old alt out and the new one in tonight. I belive it was original since the bolts where very hard to tak out. thanks again. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1.html||||reg||10
Z||000003||rogergarrison||07-12-2000||01:07 PM||||the engine compartment on Fieros get very very hot, hard on everything-including bolts. I always recomment when replacing ANYTHING bolted in use anti-seize compound so it dont freeze up in the hole. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rrazzz||07-12-2000||07:22 PM||||If you want to be sure you can remove bolts again later, you can also replace them with stainless steel - available at hardware or boat supply stores. ||||reg||1
